import References.Nag1988.Ch04.S04_SchwarzianAndDeformations

/-!
# Nag, Chapter 4 §4.5: The Bers boundary of Teichmüller space (W2 batch N3)

Source: S. Nag, *The Complex Analytic Theory of Teichmüller Spaces*, Wiley 1988, Ch. 4 §4.5 (`full.md` N2:3905–4050,
folder `The Complex Analytic Theory … c10f6cd1`).

Conventions as in `Ch04/S04_SchwarzianAndDeformations`: `Γ` is a Fuchsian group, `T_β(G) = LiZhongQC.bersImage Γ ⊆ B₂(L, G)`, `f^φ` is any
developing mapping of `φ` (`Miyachi2008.IsDevelopingMap`), `(σ^φ, f^φ)` a deformation (`IsDeformation`) with image group `G^φ = σ^φ(G)`
(`IsImageGroup`, a subgroup `H` of `SL(2, ℂ)`). The Kleinian notions are those of `Lehto1987` (`IsKleinian`, `IsElementary`, `discontinuitySet`,
`IsHyperbolicMob`, `IsParabolicMob`). The boundary `∂T_β(G)` is taken in `B₂(L, G)` for the cusp norm (`bersBoundary`); its topology for the
notions of category is the norm topology (`bersBoundaryTopology`). "`dim T(G) < ∞`" is `FiniteDimensional ℂ` of the span of `B₂(L, G)` with positive
dimension (leader ruling 6). Dimension clauses are not stated (no topological dimension in the project; leader ruling 3).

* Definition (the Bers boundary `∂T_β(G)`, §4.5.1, N2:3905) — `IsBClosurePt`, `bersBoundary`, `bersBoundaryTopology`
* Theorem 4.5.1 (for `φ ∈ ∂T_β(G)`, `f^φ` is globally schlicht and `G^φ` is Kleinian with an invariant component, N2:3909) — `thm4_5_1`
* Definition (cusp, §4.5.2, N2:3935) — `IsCusp`
* Proposition 4.5.2 (for `G` of the first kind the invariant component is `f^φ(L)`, N2:3947) — `prop4_5_2`
* Definition (totally degenerate Kleinian group and point, §4.5.2, N2:3957) — `IsTotallyDegenerate`, `IsTotallyDegeneratePt`
* Theorem 4.5.3 (most boundary points are totally degenerate: the totally degenerate points are of second category, N2:3966) — `thm4_5_3`
  (the clause "this subset has dimension equal to the dimension of `∂T_β(G)`" is not stated)
* Proposition A (the cusps form a meagre subset of `∂T_β(G)`, N2:3977) — `propA`
  (the clause "of topological dimension strictly less than the dimension of `∂T_β(G)`" is not stated)
* Proposition B (a boundary point which is not a cusp is totally degenerate, N2:3979) — `propB`
* Proposition 4.5.5 (a boundary point which is not totally degenerate: (a) the other components of `Ω(G^φ)` are not invariant; (b) the
  stabilizer of such a component contains a parabolic `γ` with `(σ^φ)⁻¹(γ)` hyperbolic, N2:3999) — `prop4_5_5_a`, `prop4_5_5_b`
* Proposition 4.5.6 (modular elements fixing the origin are Möbius `ω` of the normalizer, and extend to `∂T_β(G)` as linear isometries
  `ω*` of `B₂(L, G)`, N2:4019) — `omegaStar`, `prop4_5_6`, `prop4_5_6_mod`
* Propositions of §4.5.4 (the proof of Proposition A: the varieties `Y_g`, hyperbolic elements pinched to parabolic) — omitted: steps of the
  proof of Proposition A (the sets `Y_g`; statement of Bers' existence of cusps quoted from [B-11])

Readings: Bers' theorem `∂T_β(G)` is "closed and bounded"; the boundary is the closure of `T_β(G)` minus its interior (`T_β(G)` is open).
-/

open Complex Set Metric Filter Topology MeasureTheory
open scoped ENNReal NNReal Real ComplexConjugate MatrixGroups

noncomputable section

namespace Nag1988

open LiZhongQC (lowerHalf ExtPlane meroToExt schwarzian mobiusSL IsFuchsian bersImage IsHyperbolic)
open GardinerLakic2000 (cuspNorm cuspFormsL IsFirstKind)
open Lehto1987 (IsKleinian IsElementary discontinuitySet IsParabolicMob)
open Miyachi2008 (IsDevelopingMap)

variable {Γ : Subgroup (Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup (Fin 2) ℝ)}

/-- `φ` is in the closure of `S` for the norm of `B₂(L, G)`: for every `δ > 0` there is `ψ ∈ S` with `‖ψ − φ‖ < δ`. -/
def IsBClosurePt (S : Set (ℂ → ℂ)) (φ : ℂ → ℂ) : Prop :=
  ∀ δ : ℝ, 0 < δ → ∃ ψ ∈ S, cuspNorm lowerHalf (ψ - φ) < ENNReal.ofReal δ

/-- **The Bers boundary `∂T_β(G)`** (Ch. 4 §4.5.1, N2:3905). The boundary points of the domain `T_β(G)` in `B₂(L, G)`: the points of
`B₂(L, G)` in the closure of `T_β(G)` which are not interior points of `T_β(G)`. -/
def bersBoundary (Γ : Subgroup (Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup (Fin 2) ℝ)) : Set (ℂ → ℂ) :=
  {φ | φ ∈ cuspFormsL Γ ∧ IsBClosurePt (bersImage Γ) φ ∧ ¬ IsBInteriorPt Γ (bersImage Γ) φ}

/-- The norm topology of `B₂(L, G)` on the Bers boundary: the open sets are generated by the norm-open sets of `∂T_β(G)`. -/
@[instance_reducible]
def bersBoundaryTopology (Γ : Subgroup (Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup (Fin 2) ℝ)) : TopologicalSpace (bersBoundary Γ) :=
  TopologicalSpace.generateFrom
    {S : Set (bersBoundary Γ) | IsBOpen (cuspNorm lowerHalf) (bersBoundary Γ) (Subtype.val '' S)}

/-- **Theorem 4.5.1** (Bers; Ch. 4 §4.5.1, N2:3909). Let `φ ∈ ∂T_β(G)`, `G` an arbitrary Fuchsian group. Then `f^φ` is globally schlicht on
`L`. Consequently `σ^φ(G) = G^φ` is a Kleinian group that acts properly discontinuously on `f^φ(L)`, preserving this domain; thus `G^φ`
has an invariant component of its region of discontinuity containing `f^φ(L)`. -/
theorem thm4_5_1 {φ : ℂ → ℂ} (hφ : φ ∈ bersBoundary Γ) {σ : Γ → ExtPlane → ExtPlane} {f : ℂ → ℂ} (hd : IsDeformation Γ σ f)
    (hS : ∀ z ∈ lowerHalf, schwarzian f z = φ z) :
    InjOn (meroToExt f) lowerHalf ∧ ∀ H : Subgroup SL(2, ℂ), IsImageGroup σ H →
      IsKleinian H ∧ meroToExt f '' lowerHalf ⊆ discontinuitySet H ∧
        (∀ A ∈ H, mobiusSL A '' (meroToExt f '' lowerHalf) = meroToExt f '' lowerHalf) ∧
        ∃ C : Set ExtPlane, (∃ p ∈ discontinuitySet H, C = connectedComponentIn (discontinuitySet H) p) ∧
          meroToExt f '' lowerHalf ⊆ C ∧ ∀ A ∈ H, mobiusSL A '' C = C := by
  sorry

/-- **Cusp** (Ch. 4 §4.5.2, N2:3935). A point `φ ∈ ∂T_β(G)` is a *cusp* if there exists a hyperbolic element `g` of `G` such that
`σ^φ(g)` is parabolic. (Independent of the deformation representing `φ`.) -/
def IsCusp (Γ : Subgroup (Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup (Fin 2) ℝ)) (φ : ℂ → ℂ) : Prop :=
  φ ∈ bersBoundary Γ ∧ ∃ (σ : Γ → ExtPlane → ExtPlane) (f : ℂ → ℂ), IsDeformation Γ σ f ∧
    (∀ z ∈ lowerHalf, schwarzian f z = φ z) ∧
      ∃ g : Γ, IsHyperbolic (g : Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup (Fin 2) ℝ) ∧ ∃ A : SL(2, ℂ), mobiusSL A = σ g ∧ IsParabolicMob A

/-- **Proposition 4.5.2** (Ch. 4 §4.5.2, N2:3947). If `G` is of the first kind, then for any boundary point `φ` the component of
`Ω(G^φ)` containing `f^φ(L)` is `f^φ(L)` itself. -/
theorem prop4_5_2 (hfirst : IsFirstKind Γ) {φ : ℂ → ℂ} (hφ : φ ∈ bersBoundary Γ) {σ : Γ → ExtPlane → ExtPlane} {f : ℂ → ℂ}
    (hd : IsDeformation Γ σ f) (hS : ∀ z ∈ lowerHalf, schwarzian f z = φ z) {H : Subgroup SL(2, ℂ)} (hH : IsImageGroup σ H)
    {p : ExtPlane} (hp : p ∈ meroToExt f '' lowerHalf) :
    connectedComponentIn (discontinuitySet H) p = meroToExt f '' lowerHalf := by
  sorry

/-- **Totally degenerate Kleinian group** (Ch. 4 §4.5.2, N2:3957). A nonelementary Kleinian group `H` whose full region of discontinuity
`Ω(H)` is connected and simply connected. -/
def IsTotallyDegenerate (H : Subgroup SL(2, ℂ)) : Prop :=
  IsKleinian H ∧ ¬ IsElementary H ∧ IsConnected (discontinuitySet H) ∧ SimplyConnectedSpace ↥(discontinuitySet H)

/-- **Totally degenerate point** (Ch. 4 §4.5.3, N2:3971). `φ ∈ ∂T_β(G)` is totally degenerate if `G^φ` is a totally degenerate group
(for the image group of every deformation with Schwarzian `φ`; they are conjugate). -/
def IsTotallyDegeneratePt (Γ : Subgroup (Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup (Fin 2) ℝ)) (φ : ℂ → ℂ) : Prop :=
  φ ∈ bersBoundary Γ ∧ ∀ (σ : Γ → ExtPlane → ExtPlane) (f : ℂ → ℂ), IsDeformation Γ σ f →
    (∀ z ∈ lowerHalf, schwarzian f z = φ z) → ∀ H : Subgroup SL(2, ℂ), IsImageGroup σ H → IsTotallyDegenerate H

/-- **Theorem 4.5.3** (Bers; Ch. 4 §4.5.3, N2:3966). Let `G` be a finitely generated Fuchsian group of the first kind such that `T(G)`
is not just a singleton point. Then most points of `∂T_β(G)` represent totally degenerate groups: the subset of totally degenerate points
is of second category (non-meagre) in the compact space `∂T_β(G)`. (The clause on the topological dimension is not stated.) -/
theorem thm4_5_3 (hΓ : IsFuchsian Γ) (hfg : Group.FG Γ) (hfirst : IsFirstKind Γ)
    (hdim : FiniteDimensional ℂ (Submodule.span ℂ (cuspFormsL Γ))) (hpos : 0 < Module.finrank ℂ (Submodule.span ℂ (cuspFormsL Γ))) :
    ¬ @IsMeagre (bersBoundary Γ) (bersBoundaryTopology Γ) {x | IsTotallyDegeneratePt Γ x.1} := by
  sorry

/-- **Proposition A** (Bers; Ch. 4 §4.5.3, N2:3977). For `G` as in Theorem 4.5.3, the subset of cusps in `∂T_β(G)` is of first category
(meagre) in the compact space `∂T_β(G)`. (The clause on the topological dimension is not stated.) -/
theorem propA (hΓ : IsFuchsian Γ) (hfg : Group.FG Γ) (hfirst : IsFirstKind Γ)
    (hdim : FiniteDimensional ℂ (Submodule.span ℂ (cuspFormsL Γ))) (hpos : 0 < Module.finrank ℂ (Submodule.span ℂ (cuspFormsL Γ))) :
    @IsMeagre (bersBoundary Γ) (bersBoundaryTopology Γ) {x | IsCusp Γ x.1} := by
  sorry

/-- **Proposition B** (Bers; Ch. 4 §4.5.3, N2:3979). For `G` as in Theorem 4.5.3, every `φ ∈ ∂T_β(G)` that is not a cusp is necessarily
totally degenerate. -/
theorem propB (hΓ : IsFuchsian Γ) (hfg : Group.FG Γ) (hfirst : IsFirstKind Γ)
    (hdim : FiniteDimensional ℂ (Submodule.span ℂ (cuspFormsL Γ))) (hpos : 0 < Module.finrank ℂ (Submodule.span ℂ (cuspFormsL Γ)))
    {φ : ℂ → ℂ} (hφ : φ ∈ bersBoundary Γ) (hc : ¬ IsCusp Γ φ) : IsTotallyDegeneratePt Γ φ := by
  sorry

/-- **Proposition 4.5.5 (a)** (Bers; Ch. 4 §4.5.5, N2:3999). Let `G` be finitely generated Fuchsian of the first kind with
`0 < dim T(G) < ∞`. If `φ ∈ ∂T_β(G)` is not totally degenerate, then each component of `Ω(G^φ)` aside from `f^φ(L)` is noninvariant. -/
theorem prop4_5_5_a (hΓ : IsFuchsian Γ) (hfg : Group.FG Γ) (hfirst : IsFirstKind Γ)
    (hdim : FiniteDimensional ℂ (Submodule.span ℂ (cuspFormsL Γ))) (hpos : 0 < Module.finrank ℂ (Submodule.span ℂ (cuspFormsL Γ)))
    {φ : ℂ → ℂ} (hφ : φ ∈ bersBoundary Γ) (hnt : ¬ IsTotallyDegeneratePt Γ φ) {σ : Γ → ExtPlane → ExtPlane} {f : ℂ → ℂ}
    (hd : IsDeformation Γ σ f) (hS : ∀ z ∈ lowerHalf, schwarzian f z = φ z) {H : Subgroup SL(2, ℂ)} (hH : IsImageGroup σ H)
    {P : Set ExtPlane} (hP : ∃ p ∈ discontinuitySet H, P = connectedComponentIn (discontinuitySet H) p)
    (hne : P ≠ meroToExt f '' lowerHalf) : ∃ A ∈ H, mobiusSL A '' P ≠ P := by
  sorry

/-- **Proposition 4.5.5 (b)** (Bers; Ch. 4 §4.5.5, N2:3999). In the situation of (a), if `P` is such a (noninvariant) component, there
exists a parabolic `γ` in the stabilizer `G^φ_P` of `P` such that `(σ^φ)⁻¹(γ)` is hyperbolic in `G`. -/
theorem prop4_5_5_b (hΓ : IsFuchsian Γ) (hfg : Group.FG Γ) (hfirst : IsFirstKind Γ)
    (hdim : FiniteDimensional ℂ (Submodule.span ℂ (cuspFormsL Γ))) (hpos : 0 < Module.finrank ℂ (Submodule.span ℂ (cuspFormsL Γ)))
    {φ : ℂ → ℂ} (hφ : φ ∈ bersBoundary Γ) (hnt : ¬ IsTotallyDegeneratePt Γ φ) {σ : Γ → ExtPlane → ExtPlane} {f : ℂ → ℂ}
    (hd : IsDeformation Γ σ f) (hS : ∀ z ∈ lowerHalf, schwarzian f z = φ z) {H : Subgroup SL(2, ℂ)} (hH : IsImageGroup σ H)
    {P : Set ExtPlane} (hP : ∃ p ∈ discontinuitySet H, P = connectedComponentIn (discontinuitySet H) p)
    (hne : P ≠ meroToExt f '' lowerHalf) :
    ∃ A ∈ H, IsParabolicMob A ∧ mobiusSL A '' P = P ∧
      ∃ g : Γ, IsHyperbolic (g : Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup (Fin 2) ℝ) ∧ σ g = mobiusSL A := by
  sorry

open scoped Classical in
/-- **The action `ω*` on `B₂(L, G)`** (Ch. 4 §4.5.6, (5.4), N2:4040): `ω*(φ) = (φ ∘ ω)(ω')²` for `ω ∈ Mob(ℝ)` (it preserves `𝕃`), with
`ω'(z) = (c z + d)⁻²`; zero off `𝕃`. -/
def omegaStar (ω : Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup (Fin 2) ℝ) (φ : ℂ → ℂ) : ℂ → ℂ :=
  fun z => if z ∈ lowerHalf then φ (mobAct ω z) / ((ω 1 0 : ℂ) * z + ω 1 1) ^ 4 else 0

/-- **Proposition 4.5.6** (Ch. 4 §4.5.6, N2:4019). Any element of `Mod(G)` that fixes the origin (basepoint) of `T_β(G)` has the form
`ω*` with `ω` in the normalizer `N(G)` of `G` in `Mob(ℝ)` (Section 2.3.12), and it not only extends to `∂T_β(G)` but extends as a linear
isometry of the full ambient Banach space `B₂(L, G)`: `ω*` is a ℂ-linear norm preserving bijection of `B₂(L, G)` mapping `T_β(G)` and
`∂T_β(G)` onto themselves. -/
theorem prop4_5_6 {ω : Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup (Fin 2) ℝ} (hω : ∀ g ∈ Γ, ω * g * ω⁻¹ ∈ Γ ∧ ω⁻¹ * g * ω ∈ Γ) :
    (∀ φ ∈ cuspFormsL Γ, omegaStar ω φ ∈ cuspFormsL Γ ∧ cuspNorm lowerHalf (omegaStar ω φ) = cuspNorm lowerHalf φ) ∧
      (∀ (a : ℂ) (φ ψ : ℂ → ℂ), omegaStar ω (a • φ + ψ) = a • omegaStar ω φ + omegaStar ω ψ) ∧
        omegaStar ω '' cuspFormsL Γ = cuspFormsL Γ ∧ omegaStar ω '' bersImage Γ = bersImage Γ ∧
          omegaStar ω '' bersBoundary Γ = bersBoundary Γ := by
  sorry

/-- **Proposition 4.5.6, first assertion** (Ch. 4 §4.5.6, N2:4019; AUDIT1_Nag M1). Any element of `Mod(G)` that fixes the origin of
`T(G)` is (the class of) a Möbius transformation `ω` of the normalizer of `G` in `Mob(ℝ)`, so that it acts as `ω*` (`prop4_5_6`).
Modelling: `h ∈ QC(G)` with `ρ_h[0] = [ν]` and `[ν] = [0]` (in the relation form of `GardinerLakic2000.IsRhoGamma`: the normalized
solution of `ν` composed with the boundary map `qcBdry h` is a real Möbius map of that of the base point `μ₀ = 0`). Conclusion: the
boundary map of `h` on `ℝ` is a real Möbius map `ω`, and `ω` normalizes `G` as a group of Möbius maps (`ω g ω⁻¹ = ± g'`, `g' ∈ G`:
conjugation by `ω` may change the `SL(2, ℝ)` lift by a sign). -/
theorem prop4_5_6_mod (hΓ : IsFuchsian Γ) {h : ℂ → ℂ} (hh : h ∈ GardinerLakic2000.qcNormalizer Γ)
    (hfix : ∃ μ₀ ν : LiZhongQC.BeltramiGamma Γ, (∀ z, μ₀.1.1 z = 0) ∧ (LiZhongQC.teichSetoidGamma Γ).r ν μ₀ ∧
      ∃ A : Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup (Fin 2) ℝ, ∀ x : ℝ,
        OnePoint.map (LiZhongQC.fMuSym ν.1.1) (GardinerLakic2000.qcBdry h ((x : ℂ) : ExtPlane)) =
          mobiusSL (LiZhongQC.slRealToComplex A) ((LiZhongQC.fMuSym μ₀.1.1 x : ℂ) : ExtPlane)) :
    ∃ ω : Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup (Fin 2) ℝ,
      (∀ x : ℝ, GardinerLakic2000.qcBdry h ((x : ℂ) : ExtPlane) = mobiusSL (LiZhongQC.slRealToComplex ω) ((x : ℂ) : ExtPlane)) ∧
        ∀ g ∈ Γ, ∃ g' ∈ Γ, ω * g * ω⁻¹ = g' ∨ ω * g * ω⁻¹ = -g' := by
  sorry

end Nag1988
